package Libraries.Fabrication.Printers

use Libraries.Fabrication.Profiles.Profile

/*
The Printer class is a printer profile that a program can make with one
line, and the parent of every printer class in this package. On its own it
is a generic Marlin printer with a 220 by 220 millimeter bed, printing PLA
at safe, slow speeds. The families (BowdenPrinter, DirectDrivePrinter,
KlipperPrinter and BambuPrinter) and the models (such as CrealityEnder3)
change what their printers need.

Its start G-code is written in three parts (GetHeatGcode, GetHomeGcode and
GetPrimeGcode), so a printer class changes only the part that differs,
such as how it levels its bed.

Attribute: Example

use Libraries.Fabrication.Printers.Printer

Printer printer
printer:SetName("My printer")
printer:SetBed(235, 235, 250)
output printer:Describe()
*/
class Printer is Profile
    on create
        SetName("Generic printer")
        // No files: the G-code comes from GetStartGcode and GetEndGcode.
        Set("startGcodeFile", "")
        Set("endGcodeFile", "")
        // Common to nearly every printer (see ProfileIdeas.md). Starting
        // values: confirm with test prints before release.
        SetNumber("lineWidth", 0.45)
        SetNumber("infillDensity", 0.15)
        SetInteger("topLayers", 5)
        SetInteger("bottomLayers", 3)
        SetNumber("firstLayerFlow", 1.0)
        SetInteger("nozzleTemperature", 215)
        SetInteger("bedTemperature", 60)
        SetNumber("minLayerTime", 8)
        SetNumber("maxFlow", 12)
        SetNumber("zHop", 0.4)
        SetNumber("supportOverhangAngle", 60)
        SetNumber("retractLength", 0.8)
        SetNumber("retractSpeed", 30)
    end

    /*
    This action sets the printer's bed size and the tallest print it can
    make, in millimeters.

    Attribute: Parameter width The bed's size from left to right (X).
    Attribute: Parameter depth The bed's size from front to back (Y).
    Attribute: Parameter height The tallest print (Z).

    Attribute: Example

    use Libraries.Fabrication.Printers.BowdenPrinter

    BowdenPrinter printer
    printer:SetBed(235, 235, 250)
    */
    action SetBed(number width, number depth, number height)
        SetNumber("bedWidth", width)
        SetNumber("bedDepth", depth)
        SetNumber("bedHeight", height)
    end

    /*
    This action returns the start G-code: GetHeatGcode, GetHomeGcode and
    GetPrimeGcode, one after another. Placeholders such as {BED_TEMP} are
    filled in when the G-code is written.

    Attribute: Returns The start G-code.

    Attribute: Example

    use Libraries.Fabrication.Printers.Printer

    Printer printer
    output printer:GetStartGcode()
    */
    action GetStartGcode returns text
        text lineFeed = ""
        lineFeed = lineFeed:GetLineFeed()
        return GetHeatGcode() + lineFeed + GetHomeGcode() + lineFeed + GetPrimeGcode()
    end

    /*
    This action returns the G-code that starts heating the bed and the
    nozzle. They heat together, so homing can run while they warm.

    Attribute: Returns The heating G-code.

    Attribute: Example

    use Libraries.Fabrication.Printers.Printer

    Printer printer
    output printer:GetHeatGcode()
    */
    action GetHeatGcode returns text
        return Lines("M140 S{BED_TEMP} ;start heating the bed", "M104 S{NOZZLE_TEMP} ;start heating the nozzle")
    end

    /*
    This action returns the G-code that homes the printer, and levels the
    bed on printers whose classes add it. By default it only homes.

    Attribute: Returns The homing G-code.

    Attribute: Example

    use Libraries.Fabrication.Printers.Printer

    Printer printer
    output printer:GetHomeGcode()
    */
    action GetHomeGcode returns text
        return "G28 ;home all axes"
    end

    /*
    This action returns the G-code that waits for the heat, then draws two
    priming lines near the left edge of the bed, so the nozzle is full of
    plastic when the print starts.

    Attribute: Returns The priming G-code.

    Attribute: Example

    use Libraries.Fabrication.Printers.Printer

    Printer printer
    output printer:GetPrimeGcode()
    */
    action GetPrimeGcode returns text
        text lineFeed = ""
        lineFeed = lineFeed:GetLineFeed()
        return Lines("M190 S{BED_TEMP} ;wait for the bed", "M109 S{NOZZLE_TEMP} ;wait for the nozzle") + lineFeed
            + Lines("G90", "M83") + lineFeed
            + Lines("G1 Z2.0 F3000", "G1 X5 Y20 Z0.3 F5000") + lineFeed
            + Lines("G1 X5 Y120 E12 F1500 ;prime line", "G1 X5.4 Y120 F5000") + lineFeed
            + Lines("G1 X5.4 Y20 E12 F1500 ;prime line", "G1 Z2.0 F3000")
    end

    /*
    This action returns the end G-code: lift away from the print, bring it
    to the front, and turn the heaters, fan and motors off.

    Attribute: Returns The end G-code.

    Attribute: Example

    use Libraries.Fabrication.Printers.Printer

    Printer printer
    output printer:GetEndGcode()
    */
    action GetEndGcode returns text
        text lineFeed = ""
        lineFeed = lineFeed:GetLineFeed()
        return Lines("G91 ;relative positioning", "G1 Z10 F600 ;lift away from the print") + lineFeed
            + Lines("G90", "G1 X0 Y{PARK_Y} F6000 ;present the print") + lineFeed
            + Lines("M104 S0 ;nozzle heater off", "M140 S0 ;bed heater off") + lineFeed
            + Lines("M107 ;fan off", "M84 ;motors off")
    end

    /*
    This action joins two lines of G-code, for printer classes that build
    their G-code a few lines at a time.

    Attribute: Parameter first The first line.
    Attribute: Parameter second The second line.
    Attribute: Returns The two lines, one after the other.

    Attribute: Example

    use Libraries.Fabrication.Printers.Printer

    Printer printer
    output printer:Lines("G28 ;home all axes", "G29 ;measure the bed")
    */
    action Lines(text first, text second) returns text
        text lineFeed = ""
        lineFeed = lineFeed:GetLineFeed()
        return first + lineFeed + second
    end
end
